[ceiling] Wrong build direction for this factory tool. magnet-retention.md specifies the common Y84.269 back on the bed, with machine -Y as build-up. This Z-normal bridge face is vertical in that pose. The hash-bound factory_gauge_build_pose_review in magnet-geometry.json reads the canonical STL and finds every horizontal print-down facet on the bed.
alternatives: Printing upright in machine +Z would require supports under the bridge and could mark its registering faces. The specified flat-back pose retains the required 2.000 mm pole-setting step and places the central rib, both feet and bridge directly on the same bed plane; changing the gauge's machine-frame geometry is unnecessary.
