[thin] Wrong threshold classification at the nominal 3 mm boundary. The central rib is exactly 3.000 mm between Y81.269 and Y84.269, the bridge is exactly 3.000 mm between Z206.8554 and Z209.8554, and the side foot is exactly 3.000 mm between X−64.400 and X−61.400. The canonical STL's corresponding coordinate intervals also measure exactly 3.000 mm; these sections meet the ordinary wall dimension. The gauge_three_mm_boundary_review in magnet-geometry.json binds both surfaces and their hashes.
alternatives: Adding a small thickness solely to move an exact 3 mm wall past the classifier's numeric boundary changes the factory tool without addressing an actual thin section. The classifier should distinguish its numeric threshold from a material section below 3 mm; printed gauge accuracy remains a separate measurement.
